 # @demo/dsh-bench-status (exam material only, do not publish)
 
 A small npm **bundle plugin** sample whose Node half (the packed `lib/index.mjs`,
-the `main` entry) is written against the pre-0812 host service names: `inject` is
-`['tasks', 'httpServer']`, the task registry is read through `ctx.tasks`, the
-`/bench-status/status` route is registered through `ctx.httpServer.register`, and
-job completion is subscribed through the `onTaskDone` listener.
+the `main` entry) is a function plugin over the dsh **0.1.2-alpha.2** host
+services:
+
+- `inject` is `['jobs']` — the background-job registry read by both the open
+  count and the completion log;
+- the job registry is read through `ctx.jobs` (`jobs.list()`);
+- the `/bench-status/status` route is registered through
+  `ctx.webServer.register` and answers `{"ok":true,"open":N}`; it rides a
+  scoped `ctx.inject(['webServer', 'connection'], ...)`, so the plugin activates
+  in a composition without the web carrier (headless, ACP) and serves the route
+  wherever the web composition mounts it; a raw `webServer` route does not
+  inherit the Connection gate, so the handler calls
+  `ctx.connection.requestRejection(req)` first and answers 401/403 instead of
+  the payload when the request is rejected;
+- job completion is subscribed through the `jobs.onJobDone` listener.
+
+`cordis.patch.yml` is the bundle patch (`dsh.bundle.patch` in `package.json`)
+that mounts the plugin into the web composition.
+
+The 0812 host-service rename moved this plugin onto the current vocabulary:
+`httpServer`→`webServer`, `tasks`→`jobs`, and `onTaskDone`→`onJobDone`; the
+route-registration interface kept its shape.
 
 The host in this container is dsh **0.1.2-alpha.2**.
 
